(5225395, 757225, 89774, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PhotoInterest:</b></div><hr/><i> The blurring of Tessa''s face to highlight the glasses is really clever.  But, I''ll bet that you''re taking some flack for this score wise by the "technical junkies" in here! LOL </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re not kidding! Well, at least 1 person actually got what I was going for. I suppose that means that I wasn''t very successful. Yes, I do realise that shooting f1.8 will give very little depth of field and I enjoy playing with that - I obviously wasn''t able to pull it off very well.</td>', 'Originally posted by PhotoInterest: The blurring of Tessa''s face to highlight the glasses is really clever.  But, I''ll bet that you''re taking some flack for this score wise by the "technical junkies" in here! LOL   You''re not kidding! Well, at least 1 person actually got what I was going for. I suppose that means that I wasn''t very successful. Yes, I do realise that shooting f1.8 will give very little depth of field and I enjoy playing with that - I obviously wasn''t able to pull it off very well.', '2009-01-28 23:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
